items/thm-convex-subsets-have-trivial-fundamental-group.md-43-
items/thm-convex-subsets-have-trivial-fundamental-group.md-44-[L1] The straight-line formula between two continuous maps into a convex subset is a continuous homotopy ([[lem-straight-line-homotopies-are-continuous]]).
items/thm-convex-subsets-have-trivial-fundamental-group.md-45-
items/thm-convex-subsets-have-trivial-fundamental-group.md:46:[L2] Every nonempty contractible space is path-connected, and the published straight-line contraction makes a nonempty convex subset contractible ([[cor-contractible-spaces-are-path-connected]] and its dependency [[cor-convex-subsets-of-rn-are-contractible]]).
items/thm-convex-subsets-have-trivial-fundamental-group.md-47-
items/thm-convex-subsets-have-trivial-fundamental-group.md-48-[L3] A loop class is the identity exactly when the loop is endpoint-homotopic to the constant loop ([[def-based-loops-and-fundamental-group]], [[thm-fundamental-group-laws]]).
items/thm-convex-subsets-have-trivial-fundamental-group.md-49-
items/thm-convex-subsets-have-trivial-fundamental-group.md-50-[L4] Simple connectedness means nonempty path-connectedness and a one-element fundamental group at every basepoint ([[def-simply-connected]]).
